{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pGfH8spT8coVKYbunN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 07 is finished. Both checklist items pass their tests, and the full `npm test` (lint plus 4242 unit tests) passed before the last commit.\n\n**What changed**\n\n1. In `src/renderer/controllers/media-controller.js`, `openExternalPlayer` now keeps a way to cancel its \"server running\" subscription, and a new `playerClosed()` action calls it. The shim hands back the unsubscribe function asynchronously. So if the user leaves before it arrives, the controller remembers it was cancelled and unsubscribes as soon as the function turns up. If a reply still slips in before the subscription is gone, the listener checks whether `state.playing` is still the play it was set up for. `closePlayer` replaces that object, so a stale reply does nothing: it doesn't open the external player with an empty URL and doesn't set `isReady` on the next play.\n2. The ticket only lists the media controller, but that controller had no way to find out the player had closed. So `closePlayer` in `playback-controller.js` now dispatches `playerClosed`, and `main.js` maps that action to the media controller.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- The new file `test/unit/media-controller-external-player.js` (emitted as `.external-player-test.js`) covers five cases:\n  - the wait is set while the player is open;\n  - leaving cancels it;\n  - leaving before the shim answers still cancels it;\n  - a late reply opens nothing and doesn't touch the next play;\n  - a normal reply still opens the external player.\n- I added a test to `engine-ipc-call-sites.js` that `closePlayer` dispatches `playerClosed`. I confirmed it fails without the playback-controller change.\n- I ran the controller test files together in both orders, as the collision warning in `test/AGENTS.md` asks, and all 139 tests passed each way.\n\nI also added a short note on this cancel-before-the-subscription-resolves pattern to `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`. The notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed), including a heads-up that the playback-controller ticket will edit `closePlayer` near the new dispatch line."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":70669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":688},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11f41803-e0fe-4b16-bc79-29d66fb80fef","uuid":"128a08f3-7021-4d0e-80df-1c701c5e4364","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:14:06.370Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pGf11p1kAiY4pmfc1F"}
