e unsubscribe function asynchronously. So if the user leaves before it arrives, the controller remembers it was cancelled and unsubscribes as soon as the function turns up. If a reply still slips in before the subscription is gone, the listener checks whether `state.playing` is still the play it was set up for. `closePlayer` replaces that object, so a stale reply does nothing: it doesn't open the external player with an empty URL and doesn't set `isReady` on the next play.\n2. The ticket only lists the media controller, but that controller had no way to find out the player had closed. So `closePlayer` in `playback-controller.js` now dispatches `playerClosed`, and `main.js` maps that action to the media controller.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- The new file `test/unit/media-controller-external-player.js` (emitted as `.external-player-test.js`) covers five cases:\n  - the wait is set while the player is open;\n  - leaving cancels it;\n  - leaving before the shim answers still cancels it;\n  - a late reply opens nothing and doesn't touch the next play;\n  - a normal reply still opens the external player.\n- I added a test to `engine-ipc-call-sites.js` that `closePlayer` dispatches `playerClosed`. I confirmed it fails without the playback-controller change.\n- I ran the controller test files together in both orders, as the collision warning in `test/AGENTS.md` asks, and all 139 tests passed each way.\n\nI also added a short note on this cancel-before-the-subscription-resolves pattern to `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`. The notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed), including a heads-up that the playback-controller ticket will edit `closePlayer` near the new dispatch line.","ttft_ms":9067,"type":"result","duration_ms":274529,"uuid":"6e139737-868d-4796-9998-600292a073c2","ttft_stream_ms":8864,"time_to_request_ms":1006,"first_content_frame_ms":8864,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
